6809 FORTH v1.0
\ ============================================================
  ok\ This is the source for the ANS test harness, it is based on the
  ok\ harness originally developed by John Hayes
  ok\ (C) 1995 JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY / APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY
  ok\ MAY BE DISTRIBUTED FREELY AS LONG AS THIS COPYRIGHT NOTICE REMAINS.
  ok\ VERSION 1.1
  ok\ Revision history and possibly newer versions can be found at
  ok\ http://www.forth200x.org/tests/ttester.fs
  okMARKER MTTESTER
  okBASE @
  okHEX
  okVARIABLE ACTUAL-DEPTH \ stack record
  okCREATE ACTUAL-RESULTS 20 CELLS ALLOT
  okVARIABLE START-DEPTH
  okVARIABLE XCURSOR \ for ...}T
  okVARIABLE ERROR-XT
  ok\ TESTCOUNT/FAILCOUNT: a Forth-computed, authoritative pass/fail
  ok\ tally, read by TEST-END (defined in 00_test_prelude.fs). Added
  ok\ because the serial test runner's line-by-line "ok" wait can't
  ok\ tell a real failure from its own echo-timing: a multi-line
  ok\ colon-definition only gets ONE "ok" for the whole definition,
  ok\ not one per physical line, so the runner was reporting every
  ok\ continuation line inside one as a bogus "[FAIL] gave up after
  ok\ 0 retries" - even though every actual }T comparison in the
  ok\ file passed. TESTCOUNT/FAILCOUNT give the runner one reliable
  ok\ line to grep for at the end of each file instead of inferring
  ok\ pass/fail from per-line echo timing.
  okVARIABLE TESTCOUNT
  okVARIABLE FAILCOUNT
  ok0 TESTCOUNT !
  ok0 FAILCOUNT !
  ok: ERROR ERROR-XT @ EXECUTE ; \ for vectoring of error reporting
  ok: "FLOATING" S" FLOATING" ; \ only compiled S" in CORE
  ok: "FLOATING-STACK" S" FLOATING-STACK" ;
  ok"FLOATING" ENVIRONMENT? [IF][IF]TRUE[ELSE]FALSE[THEN][ELSE]
  okFALSE
  ok[THEN] CONSTANT HAS-FLOATING
  ok"FLOATING-STACK" ENVIRONMENT? [IF][IF]TRUE[ELSE]FALSE[THEN][ELSE] \ We don't know whether the FP stack is separate.
  okHAS-FLOATING \ If we have FLOATING, we assume it is.
  ok[THEN] CONSTANT HAS-FLOATING-STACK
  ok: EMPTY-FSTACK ;
  ok: F{ ;
  ok: F-> ;
  ok: F} ;
  ok: F...}T ;
  ok: EMPTY-STACK \ ( ... -- ) empty stack; handles underflowed stack too.
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ < IF
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ SWAP DO 0 LOOP
THEN
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ > IF
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ DO DROP LOOP
THEN
EMPTY-FSTACK ;
  ok: ERROR1 \ ( C-ADDR U -- ) display an error message
\ followed by the line that had the error.
TYPE SOURCE TYPE CR \ display line corresponding to error
EMPTY-STACK \ throw away everything else
;
  ok' ERROR1 ERROR-XT !
  ok: T{ \ ( -- ) record the pre-test depth.
DEPTH START-DEPTH ! 0 XCURSOR ! F{ ;
  ok: -> \ ( ... -- ) record depth and contents of stack.
DEPTH DUP ACTUAL-DEPTH ! \ record depth
START-DEPTH @ > IF \ if there is something on the stack
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ - 0 DO \ save them
ACTUAL-RESULTS I CELLS + !
LOOP
THEN
F-> ;
  ok: }T \ ( ... -- ) compare stack (expected) contents with saved
\ (actual) contents.
\ BUG FIX / ENHANCEMENT: tallies TESTCOUNT (every call) and
\ FAILCOUNT (only the two branches below that call ERROR) for
\ TEST-END (00_test_prelude.fs) - see TESTCOUNT's comment above.
\ Also moved the "Actual:Expected " heading to print ONCE per
\ }T, right before the per-item loop, instead of once per item -
\ it was repeating those 16 characters before every single pair,
\ which padded out already-long result lines (e.g. gd7's 7-item
\ results) a lot for no extra information.
1 TESTCOUNT +!
DEPTH ACTUAL-DEPTH @ = IF \ if depths match
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ > IF \ if something on the stack
2 SPACES ." Actual:Expected "
DEPTH START-DEPTH @ - 0 DO \ for each stack item
ACTUAL-RESULTS I CELLS + @ \ compare actual with expected
2DUP . ." =?= " .
<> IF 1 FAILCOUNT +! S" INCORRECT RESULT: " ERROR LEAVE THEN
LOOP
THEN
ELSE \ depth mismatch
1 FAILCOUNT +!
S" WRONG NUMBER OF RESULTS: " ERROR
THEN
F} ;
  ok\ TEST-BEGIN / TEST-END (the per-file report that reads TESTCOUNT
  ok\ and FAILCOUNT) are defined in 00_test_prelude.fs.
  ok' }T ." XT for }T" .7182 
  ok: ...}T ( -- )
XCURSOR @ START-DEPTH @ + ACTUAL-DEPTH @ <> IF
S" NUMBER OF CELL RESULTS BEFORE '->' DOES NOT MATCH ...}T "
S" SPECIFICATION: " ERROR
ELSE DEPTH START-DEPTH @ = 0= IF
S" NUMBER OF CELL RESULTS BEFORE AND AFTER '->' DOES NOT MATCH: "
ERROR
THEN THEN
F...}T ;
  ok: XTESTER ( X -- )
DEPTH 0= ACTUAL-DEPTH @ XCURSOR @ START-DEPTH @ + 1+ < OR IF
S" NUMBER OF CELL RESULTS AFTER '->' BELOW ...}T SPECIFICATION: "
ERROR EXIT
ELSE ACTUAL-RESULTS XCURSOR @ CELLS + @ <> IF
S" INCORRECT CELL RESULT: " ERROR
THEN THEN
1 XCURSOR +! ;
  ok: X}T XTESTER ...}T ;
  ok: XX}T XTESTER XTESTER ...}T ;
  ok: XXX}T XTESTER XTESTER XTESTER ...}T ;
  ok: XXXX}T XTESTER XTESTER XTESTER XTESTER ...}T ;
  ok\ Set the following flag to TRUE for more verbose output; this may
  ok\ allow you to tell which test caused your system to hang.
  okVARIABLE VERBOSE
  okFALSE VERBOSE !
  ok: TESTING \ ( -- ) TALKING COMMENT.
SOURCE VERBOSE @
IF DUP >R TYPE CR R> >IN !
ELSE >IN ! DROP
THEN ;
  okBASE !
  ok\ ============================================================
  ok\ 00_test_prelude.fs
  ok\ Shared prerequisites for every section's ANS test file below.
  ok\ Load ttester.fs FIRST (this file uses T{/->/}T itself, in the
  ok\ BITSSET? and MSB checks below, so it cannot load before the
  ok\ harness does), then this file, then any section file, in the
  ok\ order given by each section file's own header comment.
  ok\ Extracted from the ANS Forth Standard, Annex F: Test Suite
  ok\ (https://forth-standard.org/standard/testsuite), which is
  ok\ explicitly redistributable per its own header:
  ok\   "(C) 1995 JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY / APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY
  ok\    MAY BE DISTRIBUTED FREELY AS LONG AS THIS COPYRIGHT NOTICE
  ok\    REMAINS."
  ok\ ============================================================
  okMARKER MTPRELUDE
  okHEX
  ok\ ---- Test reporting: TEST-BEGIN / TEST-END ----
  ok\ Every test file calls TEST-BEGIN on the line after its MARKER and
  ok\ TEST-END on the line before its closing marker. Together they are
  ok\ the whole per-file report - nothing else is needed, with or without
  ok\ the Python test runner.
  ok\   TEST-BEGIN  zeroes the pass/fail counters (TESTCOUNT, FAILCOUNT,
  ok\               bumped by }T in ttester.fs) and records the data
  ok\               stack depth, so stray cells can be spotted later.
  ok\   TEST-END    prints "TEST SUMMARY: N run, M failed" (always in
  ok\               DECIMAL) then, if the file left the stack deeper than
  ok\               TEST-BEGIN found it, "STACK IMBALANCE: n extra cell(s)
  ok\               dropped" and drops them so the next file starts clean.
  ok\               (A shallower stack is reported as "cell(s) missing".)
  okVARIABLE TEST-DEPTH
  ok: TEST-BEGIN ( -- )
0 TESTCOUNT ! 0 FAILCOUNT !
DEPTH TEST-DEPTH ! ;
  ok: TEST-END ( -- )
BASE @ >R DECIMAL
CR ." TEST SUMMARY: " TESTCOUNT @ . ." run, "
FAILCOUNT @ . ." failed" CR
DEPTH TEST-DEPTH @ > IF
." STACK IMBALANCE: " DEPTH TEST-DEPTH @ - .
." extra cell(s) dropped" CR
DEPTH TEST-DEPTH @ DO DROP LOOP
THEN
DEPTH TEST-DEPTH @ < IF
." STACK IMBALANCE: " TEST-DEPTH @ DEPTH - .
." cell(s) missing" CR
THEN
R> BASE ! ;
  ok\ Report on the prelude's own checks below, too.
  okTEST-BEGIN
  ok\ ---- F.3.1 Basic Assumptions ----
  okT{ -> }T                        \ Start with a clean slate
  okT{ : BITSSET? IF 0 0 ELSE 0 THEN ; -> }T
  okT{ 0 BITSSET? -> 0 }T  Actual:Expected 0 =?= 0 
  okT{ 1 BITSSET? -> 0 0 }T  Actual:Expected 0 =?= 0 0 =?= 0 
  okT{ -1 BITSSET? -> 0 0 }T  Actual:Expected 0 =?= 0 0 =?= 0 
  ok\ ---- F.3.2 Booleans (needs AND, INVERT tested first - section 16) ----
  ok\ 0S and 1S themselves are NOT defined anywhere else in this harness -
  ok\ every later section (including F.3.5 below, which builds <FALSE>/
  ok\ <TRUE> from them) depends on them existing first. Standard meaning:
  ok\ 0S is the single-cell all-zero-bits value, 1S is single-cell
  ok\ all-one-bits (i.e. -1) - matches their use at F.3.3 below, where
  ok\ "1S 1 RSHIFT INVERT" must yield the sign bit (MSB) alone.
  ok0 CONSTANT 0S
  ok0 INVERT CONSTANT 1S
  ok\ ---- F.3.3 Shifts ----
  ok1S 1 RSHIFT INVERT CONSTANT MSB
  okT{ MSB BITSSET? -> 0 0 }T  Actual:Expected 0 =?= 0 0 =?= 0 
  ok\ ---- F.3.5 Comparisons - upper/lower bound constants ----
  ok0 INVERT CONSTANT MAX-UINT
  ok0 INVERT 1 RSHIFT CONSTANT MAX-INT
  ok0 INVERT 1 RSHIFT INVERT CONSTANT MIN-INT
  ok0 INVERT 1 RSHIFT CONSTANT MID-UINT
  ok0 INVERT 1 RSHIFT INVERT CONSTANT MID-UINT+1
  ok0S CONSTANT <FALSE>
  ok1S CONSTANT <TRUE>
  ok\ ---- F.3.10 Division - floored vs symmetric conditional compilation ----
  ok: IFFLOORED [ -3 2 / -2 = INVERT ] LITERAL IF POSTPONE \ THEN ;
  ok: IFSYM [ -3 2 / -1 = INVERT ] LITERAL IF POSTPONE \ THEN ;
  ok\ ---- F.3.19 Number Patterns - string compare (String word set assumed absent) 
  ok: S= ( ADDR1 C1 ADDR2 C2 -- T/F ) \ Compare two strings.
>R SWAP R@ = IF \ Make sure strings have same length
R> ?DUP IF \ If non-empty strings
0 DO
OVER C@ OVER C@ - IF 2DROP <FALSE> UNLOOP EXIT THEN
SWAP CHAR+ SWAP CHAR+
LOOP
THEN
2DROP <TRUE> \ If we get here, strings match
ELSE
R> DROP 2DROP <FALSE> \ Lengths mismatch
THEN ;
  ok24 CONSTANT MAX-BASE \ BASE 2 ... 36
  ok: COUNT-BITS
0 0 INVERT BEGIN DUP WHILE >R 1+ R> 2* REPEAT DROP ;
  okCOUNT-BITS 2* CONSTANT #BITS-UD \ NUMBER OF BITS IN UD
  ok\ ---- F.3.20 Memory Movement - shared buffers (FILL must run before MOVE) ----
  okCREATE FBUF 00 C, 00 C, 00 C,
  okCREATE SBUF 12 C, 34 C, 56 C,
  ok: SEEBUF FBUF C@ FBUF CHAR+ C@ FBUF CHAR+ CHAR+ C@ ;
  ok\ Deliberately NOT followed by DECIMAL - confirmed against the
  ok\ authoritative Annex F source, which stays in HEX for the rest of
  ok\ the file after this preliminary section. A trailing DECIMAL here
  ok\ previously broke ambient-HEX for every section file that assumes
  ok\ it (several use bare hex literals like F, 8000, 7F with no local
  ok\ HEX call of their own).
  ok\ Report on the prelude's own checks and trim any stray cells.
  okTEST-END
TEST SUMMARY: 6 run, 0 failed

  ok